==English==

===Etymology===
From an alteration of ''rascallion'', a fanciful elaboration of [[rascal]] (someone who is naughty). also called a, " WILD SNORT- EEEEEEE"  in some circles has been referred to in ancient greek texts as, " the one racist who doesn't know what purpal dranq is."

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɹæpˈskæljən/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

